(   - Both `for` and `while` loops support an optional `else` block.) Tj
T*
(   - Critical Semantic Rule: The `else` block executes ONLY if the loop finishes all iterations) Tj
T*
(   naturally without encountering an explicit `break` statement.) Tj
T*
(   - Ideal for search algorithms \(e.g. searching for a threshold violation; if no item breaks the) Tj
T*
(   loop, `else` logs 'All samples within safe tolerance'\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
