12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Functions in Python: definition, parameter vs argument distinction, positional, keyword, default, *args, and **kwargs.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Functions encapsulate reusable units of executable logic:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Parameter Specifications & Argument Passing:) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   def configure_dsp_filter\(cutoff_freq, sample_rate=44100, *filter_coeffs, **metadata\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f'Cutoff: {cutoff_freq} Hz, Sampling: {sample_rate} Hz'\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f'Additional Coefficients: {filter_coeffs}'\) # tuple) Tj
T*
(   print\(f'Metadata Specs: {metadata}'\) # dictionary) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Argument Passing Taxonomy:) Tj
T*
(   1. Positional Arguments: Mapped in order: `configure_dsp_filter\(1000, 48000\)`.) Tj
T*
(   2. Default Arguments: Optional parameters initialized with fallback defaults if omitted. Must) Tj
T*
(   follow non-default arguments.) Tj
T*
(   3. Arbitrary Positional Arguments \(`*args`\): Collects excess positional arguments into an) Tj
T*
(   immutable tuple.) Tj
T*
(   4. Arbitrary Keyword Arguments \(`**kwargs`\): Collects excess named keyword pairs into a) Tj
T*
(   dictionary.) Tj
T*
(   5. Keyword-Only Arguments \(`*` separator\): Arguments placed after a bare `*` MUST be explicitly) Tj
T*
(   passed by name: `def setup\(*, port, baud\):`.) Tj
T*
(   6. Positional-Only Arguments \(`/` separator, PEP 570\): Arguments placed before `/` must) Tj
T*
(   strictly be passed by position.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
