12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze Recursion in Python: mechanics, call stack frames, base cases, recursion depth limits, and the Divide-and-Conquer paradigm.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Recursion occurs when a function invokes itself to break a complex problem into self-similar) Tj
T*
(   subproblems:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Anatomy of Recursive Execution:) Tj
T*
(   1. Base Case: The terminating condition that returns a direct result without further recursive) Tj
T*
(   calls, preventing infinite recursion.) Tj
T*
(   2. Recursive Step: Reduces problem parameters toward the base case.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Call Stack & Memory Footprint:) Tj
T*
(   Each recursive invocation allocates a new `PyFrameObject` on the CPython call stack containing) Tj
T*
(   local variables and return address pointers. Deep recursion consumes substantial memory \($O\(N\)$) Tj
T*
(   space complexity\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Recursion Limit Safety:) Tj
T*
(   CPython guards against hardware stack overflows by enforcing a default recursion limit of 1000) Tj
T*
(   frames \(`sys.getrecursionlimit\(\)`\). Exceeding this raises a `RecursionError`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Divide-and-Conquer Example \(Fast Exponentiation in $O\(\\log N\)$\):) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   def power\(base, exp\):) Tj
T*
(   if exp == 0: return 1) Tj
T*
(   if exp % 2 == 0:) Tj
T*
(   half = power\(base, exp // 2\)) Tj
T*
(   return half * half) Tj
T*
(   return base * power\(base, exp - 1\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
(   Calculates $2^{1024}$ in only 10 recursive steps rather than 1024 steps!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Memoization and Dynamic Programming in Python using functools.lru_cache to optimize recursive algorithms.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Naive recursive functions often solve identical subproblems repeatedly, causing explosive) Tj
T*
(   exponential $O\(2^N\)$ time complexity:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Problem \(Naive Fibonacci\):) Tj
T*
(   Computing `fib\(5\)` computes `fib\(4\)` and `fib\(3\)`. Computing `fib\(4\)` also computes `fib\(3\)`.) Tj
T*
