(   As $N$ grows, the call tree doubles, making `fib\(40\)` require over 2 billion calls!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Solution: Memoization via `@functools.lru_cache`:) Tj
T*
(   Caches the return value of each function call mapped to its input arguments in a hash table:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   from functools import lru_cache) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   @lru_cache\(maxsize=None\) # Unlimited cache size) Tj
T*
(   def fibonacci\(n\):) Tj
T*
(   if n < 2: return n) Tj
T*
(   return fibonacci\(n - 1\) + fibonacci\(n - 2\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(fibonacci\(100\)\) # Computes instantly in O\(N\) linear time!) Tj
T*
(   print\(fibonacci.cache_info\(\)\) # Displays hits, misses, maxsize, currsize) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
(   Transforms intractable exponential algorithms into lightning-fast linear algorithms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
