12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Lambda Functions and Functional Programming primitives in Python: map\(\), filter\(\), and reduce\(\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Python supports functional programming paradigms where functions are first-class citizens:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Lambda Functions \(Anonymous Inline Functions\):) Tj
T*
(   Defined via `lambda arguments: expression`. The body is strictly restricted to a single) Tj
T*
(   expression whose evaluated value is returned automatically.) Tj
T*
(   `attenuate = lambda v, gain: v * \(10 ** \(gain / 20.0\)\)`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Higher-Order Functional Primitives:) Tj
T*
(   - `map\(func, iterable\)`: Lazily applies `func` to every element, yielding transformed values.) Tj
T*
(   - `filter\(predicate, iterable\)`: Lazily extracts elements for which `predicate\(item\)` evaluates) Tj
T*
(   to True.) Tj
T*
(   - `reduce\(func, iterable, initializer\)` \(from `functools`\): Sequentially folds elements into a) Tj
T*
(   cumulative scalar accumulator.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Signal Processing Pipeline Example:) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   from functools import reduce) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   adc_readings = [12, 45, 88, 105, 32, 19, 94]) Tj
T*
(   # 1. Filter: select samples above noise threshold \(> 30\)) Tj
T*
(   signals = filter\(lambda x: x > 30, adc_readings\)) Tj
T*
(   # 2. Map: convert raw ADC codes to voltage \(V = code * 5.0 / 1023\)) Tj
T*
(   voltages = map\(lambda code: code * 5.0 / 1023.0, signals\)) Tj
T*
(   # 3. Reduce: calculate total cumulative signal power sum\(V^2\)) Tj
T*
(   total_power = reduce\(lambda acc, v: acc + \(v ** 2\), voltages, 0.0\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f'Total Signal Energy: {total_power:.4f} V^2'\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
