(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Python Decorators \(@decorator\), function wrapping, functools.wraps, and parameterized decorators.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   A decorator is a callable that accepts a function as input, extends its behavior, and returns a) Tj
T*
(   modified callable wrapper:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Anatomy of a Benchmark / Execution Timer Decorator:) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   import time) Tj
T*
(   from functools import wraps) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def benchmark\(func\):) Tj
T*
(   @wraps\(func\) # Copies __name__, __doc__, and signature from original func) Tj
T*
(   def wrapper\(*args, **kwargs\):) Tj
T*
(   start_time = time.perf_counter\(\)) Tj
T*
(   result = func\(*args, **kwargs\)) Tj
T*
(   end_time = time.perf_counter\(\)) Tj
T*
(   elapsed = \(end_time - start_time\) * 1000 # milliseconds) Tj
T*
(   print\(f'[BENCHMARK] {func.__name__}\(\) took {elapsed:.4f} ms'\)) Tj
T*
(   return result) Tj
T*
(   return wrapper) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   @benchmark) Tj
T*
(   def run_dsp_fft\(samples\):) Tj
T*
(   """Computes Discrete Fourier Transform.""") Tj
T*
(   time.sleep\(0.05\) # Simulated compute) Tj
T*
(   return sum\(samples\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Parameterized Decorators \(3-tier nesting\):) Tj
T*
(   `@repeat\(num_times=3\)` wraps the decorator inside an outer factory function that accepts) Tj
T*
(   configuration arguments and returns the actual decorator callable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
