/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 9:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Generator Functions and the yield statement, contrasting eager memory lists with lazy generator evaluation in streaming sensor data.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Generators implement lazy evaluation, producing items on-demand one at a time rather than) Tj
T*
(   allocating complete collections in RAM:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Memory Challenge in Streaming ECE Telemetry:) Tj
T*
(   Capturing 100,000,000 high-frequency ADC samples into a standard Python list requires over 800) Tj
T*
(   MB of system RAM, causing low-memory microcontrollers or single-board computers to crash with) Tj
T*
(   `MemoryError`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Generator Solution:) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   def sensor_stream_generator\(total_samples\):) Tj
T*
(   sample_id = 0) Tj
T*
(   while sample_id < total_samples:) Tj
T*
(   # Yield one sample at a time; execution pauses until next\(\) is called) Tj
T*
(   yield {'id': sample_id, 'voltage': 3.3 * \(sample_id % 1024\) / 1023.0}) Tj
T*
(   sample_id += 1) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

