(   [Problem Statement]: Describe Iterators and the Python Iterator Protocol: __iter__\(\) and __next__\(\) methods, and custom iterator classes.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Iterator Protocol is the foundational mechanism governing all looping and comprehensions in) Tj
T*
(   Python:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Two Protocol Methods:) Tj
T*
(   1. `__iter__\(\)`: Returns the iterator object itself. Required for an object to be used in `for`) Tj
T*
(   loops.) Tj
T*
(   2. `__next__\(\)`: Returns the next value in the sequence. When the sequence is exhausted, it) Tj
T*
(   must raise a `StopIteration` exception.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Custom Engineering Sensor Range Iterator Class:) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   class FrequencySweep:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, start_hz, stop_hz, step_hz\):) Tj
T*
(   self.current = start_hz) Tj
T*
(   self.stop = stop_hz) Tj
T*
(   self.step = step_hz) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __iter__\(self\):) Tj
T*
(   return self) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __next__\(self\):) Tj
T*
(   if self.current > self.stop:) Tj
T*
(   raise StopIteration) Tj
T*
(   val = self.current) Tj
T*
(   self.current += self.step) Tj
T*
(   return val) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   sweep = FrequencySweep\(1000, 5000, 1000\)) Tj
T*
(   for freq in sweep:) Tj
T*
(   print\(f'Testing filter at {freq} Hz'\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
