(   1. Infinite Iterators:) Tj
T*
(   - `itertools.count\(start=0, step=1\)`: Infinite arithmetic progression \(e.g., continuous sample) Tj
T*
(   numbering\).) Tj
T*
(   - `itertools.cycle\(iterable\)`: Cycles endlessly through an iterable \(e.g., repeating a periodic) Tj
T*
(   waveform bit pattern `0b1010`\).) Tj
T*
(   - `itertools.repeat\(elem, n\)`: Repeats an element `n` times.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Terminating & Combinatorial Iterators:) Tj
T*
(   - `itertools.chain\(*iterables\)`: Chains multiple distinct streams into a single contiguous) Tj
T*
(   stream without copying.) Tj
T*
(   - `itertools.islice\(iterable, start, stop, step\)`: Slices an iterator lazily without consuming) Tj
T*
(   memory.) Tj
T*
(   - `itertools.combinations\(iterable, r\)`: Generates all $r$-length combinations of elements) Tj
T*
(   without replacement \(used for testing all resistor pairing combinations\).) Tj
T*
(   - `itertools.product\(*iterables\)`: Cartesian product \(nested for-loops in a single generator\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
