(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the functools module: partial\(\), reduce\(\), lru_cache\(\), and total_ordering\(\) with engineering implementations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The `functools` module provides higher-order functions that manipulate or return callable) Tj
T*
(   functions:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. `functools.partial\(func, *args, **keywords\)`:) Tj
T*
(   Freezes a portion of a function's arguments to create a specialized child function:) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   from functools import partial) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def analog_read\(v_ref, resolution, adc_code\):) Tj
T*
(   return \(adc_code / \(\(1 << resolution\) - 1\)\) * v_ref) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Specialize for 10-bit ADC with 3.3V reference) Tj
T*
(   read_stm32_adc = partial\(analog_read, 3.3, 10\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(read_stm32_adc\(512\)\) # 1.65 V) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. `functools.total_ordering`:) Tj
T*
(   A class decorator that automatically generates all comparison methods \(`__le__`, `__gt__`,) Tj
T*
(   `__ge__`\) when only `__eq__` and one ordering method \(`__lt__`\) are defined.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. `functools.lru_cache`: Implements least-recently-used memoization caches.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
