(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the Call Stack, Frame Objects \(PyFrameObject\), and Stack Unwinding during Exception Propagation in CPython.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   When a Python function is invoked, CPython creates a `PyFrameObject` on the call stack:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Anatomy of a PyFrameObject:) Tj
T*
(   - Local variables array \(`f_localsplus`\): Direct fast indexed array of local variables.) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluation Stack: Operand stack used for bytecode math evaluations.) Tj
T*
(   - Instruction Pointer \(`f_lasti`\): Tracks the currently executing bytecode instruction.) Tj
T*
(   - Back Pointer \(`f_back`\): Pointer to the caller's frame object, forming the stack trace chain.) Tj
T*
ET

