(   Unlike C++ or Java, Python does not support native function signature overloading where) Tj
T*
(   multiple functions share the same name with different parameter lists \(subsequent `def`) Tj
T*
(   definitions overwrite previous ones\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Python Overloading Alternatives:) Tj
T*
(   1. Default & Variable Arguments: Handling optional parameters inside a single unified function.) Tj
T*
(   2. Single-Dispatch Generic Functions \(`@functools.singledispatch`\):) Tj
T*
(   Enables function overloading based on the data type of the first argument:) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   from functools import singledispatch) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   @singledispatch) Tj
T*
(   def process_sensor_data\(data\):) Tj
T*
(   raise NotImplementedError\('Unsupported data type'\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   @process_sensor_data.register\(int\)) Tj
T*
(   @process_sensor_data.register\(float\)) Tj
T*
(   def _\(data\):) Tj
T*
(   return f'Processing scalar voltage: {data:.2f} V') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   @process_sensor_data.register\(list\)) Tj
T*
(   def _\(data\):) Tj
T*
(   return f'Processing batch array of {len\(data\)} samples') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(process_sensor_data\(3.3\)\) # Scalar voltage) Tj
T*
(   print\(process_sensor_data\([1.1, 2.2, 3.3]\)\) # Batch array) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
