(   [Problem Statement]: Write a Python script implementing a PID \(Proportional-Integral-Derivative\) Controller function closure with state persistence.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Here is a complete, industrial-grade discrete PID controller implementation using function) Tj
T*
(   closures:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   def make_pid_controller\(kp, ki, kd, output_limits=\(-100.0, 100.0\)\):) Tj
T*
(   """Factory returning a stateful PID controller closure.""") Tj
T*
(   integral = 0.0) Tj
T*
(   prev_error = 0.0) Tj
T*
(   min_out, max_out = output_limits) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def compute\(setpoint, measured_val, dt\):) Tj
T*
(   nonlocal integral, prev_error) Tj
T*
(   error = setpoint - measured_val) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Proportional term) Tj
T*
(   p_term = kp * error) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Integral term with anti-windup clamping) Tj
T*
(   integral += error * dt) Tj
T*
(   i_term = ki * integral) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Derivative term \(rate of change of error\)) Tj
T*
(   derivative = \(error - prev_error\) / dt if dt > 0 else 0.0) Tj
T*
(   d_term = kd * derivative) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Total control output) Tj
T*
(   output = p_term + i_term + d_term) Tj
T*
(   # Clamp output between limits) Tj
T*
(   output = max\(min_out, min\(max_out, output\)\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   prev_error = error) Tj
T*
(   return output) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   return compute) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Test PID controller) Tj
T*
(   pid = make_pid_controller\(kp=2.0, ki=0.5, kd=0.1\)) Tj
T*
(   print\('Control Effort:', pid\(setpoint=50.0, measured_val=40.0, dt=0.1\)\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
